        <fullName>X05_Service_Case_Information_Retrieval_16j786386e795e8</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>Facilitates the retrieval of detailed on-screen service case and invoice information. This includes analyzing and explaining customer invoices, identifying discrepancies, and addressing invoice-related inquiries alongside service case details.  Also retrieve the customer&apos;s invoice information along with invoice details in order to analyze, understand, and explain the customer to the user. Ensures that all interactions and retrievals are limited to the client associated with the active service case to maintain focus and accuracy.</description>
        <developerName>X05_Service_Case_Information_Retrieval_16j786386e795e8</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When the user&apos;s query references invoices, billing periods, or payment discrepancies, prioritize searching for invoice details and related service case information. Provide a clear explanation of the findings and confirm whether additional invoice-related assistance is required.</description>
            <developerName>instructions_0_1774615476916</developerName>
            <language>en_US</language>
            <masterLabel>instructions_0_1774615476916</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When comparing invoices, the agent must not consider credits, renegotiation
values, payment‑in‑excess adjustments, or any similar financial entries 
that appear only in the previous invoice as the cause of a higher amount 
in the current invoice. These items belong to past billing cycles and must 
be ignored when identifying the reason for an increase. Only differences 
directly appearing in the current invoice — such as late payment penalties, 
interest, service changes or new charges — should be treated as valid causes.</description>
            <developerName>instructions_0_1774615565789</developerName>
            <language>en_US</language>
            <masterLabel>instructions_0_1774615565789</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When analyzing invoices and explaining value differences to the user, always follow a consistent and structured reasoning process based on objective, observable information extracted from the invoice details.
Always compare the invoice selected by the user with the immediately preceding invoice that belongs to the same billing cycle sequence.
Identify any differences between the invoices by analyzing only what is directly and explicitly shown in the invoice data, focusing on:
   – Financial adjustments
   – Payment behavior
   – Service changes
   – Category variations
   – New charges or missing credits
Prioritize objective financial events when interpreting invoice value variations. Financial adjustments should always be evaluated carefully, as they can significantly impact the invoice amount.
Do not treat recurring or unchanged items — such as standard service bundles, monthly subscriptions, or recurring content — as the cause of value variation when they appear identically across invoices.
Avoid associating invoice differences with unrelated adjustments or historical information that does not belong to the invoice being analyzed, unless the data explicitly indicates a connection to the current cycle.
Highlight the specific, factual element that caused the value difference. When relevant, consider:
   – Payment timing or payment behavior
   – Presence or absence of financial adjustments
   – Addition or removal of services
   – Category-level differences
   – Unusual or exceptional items
When explaining discrepancies to the user, provide a clear, concise, and neutral interpretation that reflects only what the invoice data supports.
Never infer or assume causes that are not directly supported by the invoice details. Base all conclusions strictly on observable differences.</description>
            <developerName>instructions_0_1774616071792</developerName>
            <language>en_US</language>
            <masterLabel>instructions_0_1774616071792</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
